The omitted-scene card is cluttered webpage chrome — a pill reading '0.3 pgs CUT', a text button reading 'View Cut Text', a dotted rule when open. Redesign it quiet, the Apple way: at rest the line is only the word OMITTED in muted ink; hovering the line reveals a small chevron at the column's trailing edge and a gentle highlight; clicking the chevron opens the cut text inline, clicking again puts it away. The cut length leaves the page — it already lives in the Navigator row's trailing column (SceneRow.cutPages), and joins the hover tooltip and the VoiceOver label. No dotted rule.